          "text": "{\"occurrence_id\":\"flaubert-madame-bovary-06903c63a2d7\",\"core_classification\":{\"label_support\":{\"truth_conditional\":3,\"performative\":0,\"exclamatory_reflexive\":4,\"other\":0},\"confidence\":0.96,\"analysis\":\"The mother's repeated « comme je t’aime ! » both avows her love and, more prominently, expresses it in an emotionally heightened, exclamatory outburst. Nothing indicates that the utterance undertakes a commitment or has force outside T/E.\",\"ambiguity\":\"The main overlap is between a sincere truth-conditional avowal and an exclamation whose intensified form foregrounds immediate emotion; both forces are substantially present.\"},\"other_diagnosis\":{\"tpe_failure\":null,\"core_not_context\":null},\"utterance_status\":{\"status\":\"direct\",\"description\":\"The highlighted words are the mother's second directly spoken « comme je t’aime ! », addressed to her daughter and repeated in the same speech turn.\"},\"contextual_interpretation\":\"The mother calls for her daughter, rushes to embrace her, addresses her compassionately as « ma pauvre enfant », and repeats the declaration with exclamation marks. The embrace, repetition, and « comme » construction strongly frame the utterance as an immediate surge of maternal affection, while its ordinary assertion of love remains intact. The passage supplies no distinct undertaking or promise.\" ,\"evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"e1\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"« Comme je t’aime, ma pauvre enfant! comme je t’aime! »\",\"supports\":\"The literal declaration supports truth-conditional avowal, while repetition, exclamation marks, and the intensifying « comme » strongly support exclamatory/reflexive force.\",\"confidence\":0.99},{\"evidence_id\":\"e2\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"« dit sa mère se précipitant pour l’embrasser »\",\"supports\":\"The mother's rush to embrace her daughter presents the words as an emotionally activated expression of maternal affection rather than a relational undertaking.\",\"confidence\":0.98},{\"evidence_id\":\"e3\",\"source\":\"supplied_metadata\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"The matched span is the final « je t’aime » in the supplied French context from Gustave Flaubert's Madame Bovary.\",\"supports\":\"Identifies the classified occurrence as the second declaration in a repeated direct utterance.\",\"confidence\":1.0}],\"background_knowledge\":{\"used\":false,\"familiarity\":\"none\",\"confidence\":null,\"contribution\":null},\"ontology_assessment\":{\"fit\":\"natural\",\"diagnosis\":\"A combination of strong E and substantial T naturally captures the core force; no residual aspect requires O.\",\"candidate_recurrent_dimension\":null},\"notes\":\"The highlighted match is the second « je t’aime » in the repeated exclamation.\"}"
        }
